{
  "about": "Change case on both phones (Android TextCase, iOS ChangeCase), a character at a time in the design language's rules (language, a BCP-47 tag). Title Case: a letter starts a word when the character before it is no letter or digit, nor an apostrophe (' or ’) straight after a letter or digit; it is upper case and every other letter lower case. Sentence case: going back from a letter over what is not a letter or digit, the start, a line break, or a '.', '!' or '?' with at least one space between it and the letter starts a sentence and is upper case; every other letter is lower case. A digit is a decimal digit only (not ² or ½). Where words and sentences start is read from all of the words, not only the ones changed. `rows`: words as they read, the UTF-16 range changed (start, end; null for all of them) and what each of the four makes of them. `changed`: a box's words as stored, style markers and all, the stretch selected (start until end in the stored words; start == end is the whole box), one transform, and the stored words and spans after — spans move with their words. `caps`: boxes with a span's \"caps\" and the words they are drawn as. Shared row for row by both phones' tests (Android ChangeCaseTest, iOS ChangeCaseTests).",
